.TH "SERIAL.GETPORTS" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Serial.getPorts \- Serial: getPorts() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]getPorts()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]Serial\f[R]
interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an array of
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] objects representing serial ports connected to the
host which the origin has permission to access.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getPorts()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an array of
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] objects.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]SecurityError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
The returned \f[CR]Promise\f[R] rejects with this error in either of the
following situations:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[CR]serial\f[R] Permissions Policy blocks the use of this feature.
.IP \(bu 2
A user permission prompt was denied.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example uses \f[CR]getPorts()\f[R] to initialize a list of
available ports.
.IP
.EX
navigator.serial.getPorts().then((ports) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Initialize the list of available ports with \(gaports\(ga on page load.\f[R]
});
.EE
